1. Change

  `harness/model-guide/review-run.sh` gains the probe mode of spec D14 (PM
  2026-11-18). `--probe` makes exactly one call on the first control diff,
  the first diff of the set whose key holds no plant. It writes one record
  under `<private>/probes/<set_id>/` and no pass record and no raw output.
  It prints one line `<route> reachable|unreachable|region-blocked <error
  line or ->` on stdout. It exits 0 for `reachable` and 3 for the two error
  states. A probe blocked by the 70 % quota rule or by the credential scan
  is a refusal: exit 2, one `review-run:` line on stdout, no call, and no
  record. A held lock keeps the lock refusal: exit 2, one line on stderr.

  The pass and probe records gain the token log of spec D13 (PM 2026-11-18).
  The runner reads each `{"type":"step-finish","tokens":...}` event of the
  json output. The record holds `tokens` with `input`, `output`,
  `reasoning`, `cache_read`, `cache_write`, and `total`, where `total` is
  the sum of the five parts. Each entry of `diffs` holds its `id` and its
  own `tokens` object. A call with no token field adds 0 and sets
  `tokens_complete` false.

  `harness/model-guide/routes.json` holds the six rows of spec D12 and none
  of the three removed routes: Kimi, GLM 5.3, and StepFun (nvidia).

  The model call is a background job with a watcher that stops the call when
  the runner dies without its trap, for example on SIGKILL. The load watch
  of the committed `review-run.test.ts` (P5 kills the probe holder) requires
  this; without it, the fake child of the killed probe stays alive and the
  file fails its afterAll scan. No other behavior changes.

  No test file changed. `harness/opencode-credential.sh` and
  `harness/opencode-host.sh` did not change.

